<p>
This post is for five types of people:
</p>

<ul class="org-ul">
<li>The tiny group ofq Emacs users exploring dictation and voice control: let's bounce ideas around and see how far we can take this</li>
<li>Emacs users who are curious about speech: there are plenty of non-Emacs dictation tools like OpenWhispr and Superwhisper, but it might be worth the effort to make Emacs the center of your speech workflow</li>
<li>People who use dictation and voice control with other editors (Cursorless on VS Code, etc.): borrow ideas and share what you've come up with</li>
<li>People who haven't checked on the state of local speech recognition and who might be pleasantly surprised by what it can do these days</li>
<li>Me, so I can think about the things I want to experiment with and prioritize what I want to squeeze into these last two weeks before <a href="https://emacsconf.org/organizers-notebook/">EmacsConf</a> (aaah!)</li>
</ul>

</div>

